/target
# Snapshots land in the working directory; the ones in docs/ are tracked.
/*.png
# Frames dumped when checking against tests/golden/frames.sha256. All ten of
# them: the recipe in that file writes one per pinned flight, and this list has
# now fallen behind that recipe twice. `warp.txt` and `side.txt` arrived with
# the flights that widened the reference, `orbit.txt` with the one that swung
# the camera off the beam, `ansi256.txt` with the one that pinned the
# palette-index writer, `astern.txt` with the one that got behind the ship,
# `steer.txt` with the one that put a hand on the stick, and `drift.txt` with
# the one that gave that hand the camera as well, and `ahead.txt` with the one
# that got in *front* of the ship with the drive spooled up — each time leaving
# the documented regeneration recipe with an untracked file waiting to be swept
# into somebody's next `git add .`.
# An eleventh flight means an eleventh line here.
/truecolor.txt
/ascii.txt
/ansi256.txt
/warp.txt
/side.txt
